[00:03.58] Without a song I left the city
[00:43.54] Borrowed a car with no radio
[00:51.56] Gone before the sun had a chance to shine
[01:00.70] The free wind weighed on my mind
[01:10.18] How many roads begin under dark umbrella
[01:26.58] They can see the memory of love
[01:41.96] Comes a tune, clearing way like a siren
[02:33.00] Shifting soon every thought in my head
[02:40.18] 'Til they all get tangled up in blue
[02:50.24] This melody promises me someday words will come
[03:07.50] And when they do, I'll shape them into a song
